  "modified": "2026-08-14T13:48:25Z",
  "summary": "nolimit-agent ships heavily obfuscated modules with child_process + HTTP POST exfiltration pattern",
  "details": "The package ships ~49 heavily obfuscated JavaScript files under a hidden.ad/ directory using `_0x[a-f0-9]+` identifier mangling characteristic of javascript-obfuscator output. File names (advanced-evasion.js, from-generator.js, phone-validator.js, proxy-validator.js, sms-providers.js, smtp-health-cache.js, socks-loader.js, web-command.js, and 40+ single/double-letter x*.js modules) describe SMS/SMTP/SOCKS/proxy tooling that does not correspond to any documented library purpose. The file.ad/x0.js combines `require('child_process')` with HTTP POST calls carrying `hostname` and `id` fields, matching the shape of a host-identifier beacon that spawns local processes and reports results to a remote endpoint. Concealment in a dot-prefixed directory, uniform obfuscation across the entire code surface, and the child_process + POST + hostname combination are inconsistent with legitimate library behavior and consistent with an SMS/spam/abuse framework with host-callback capability.",
